Alex Chen: Quick note: our Next.js sample (next-starter-alt) tripped the eval harness due to different auth retry semantics between JS and Python SDKs. Repro steps below.

Alex Chen: Local repro: set REDWOOD_TEST_EXPIRE_MS=1000, start dev server, wait 2s, call /api/chat. JS client returns 401 and aborts, python client refreshes and retries.

Alex Chen: Snippet from pages/api/chat.js:```js
const out = await redwood.chat.create({ messages });
// sometimes throws AuthError 401 and we don't auto-retry
```

Maya Patel: saw same failure in CI on ubuntu-latest runner. Log snippet: "AuthError: 401 unauthorized, refresh failed: no retry scheduled"

Samir Gupta: Also reproduced in the LlamaIndex sample app where embedding warmup calls get a transient 401. JS path gives up, causing our eval rerun to mark regression.

Elena Rosa: Likely cause: JS SDK's interceptor doesn't block subsequent requests while a token refresh is in-flight, so multiple requests race and some see invalid token. Fix approach: queue pending requests and drain after refresh completes.

Elena Rosa: Proposed minimal change in sdk/http.ts:```js
if (resp.status === 401 && !opts._alreadyRetried) {
  if (!auth.isRefreshing) {
    auth.isRefreshing = true;
    await auth.refreshToken();
    auth.isRefreshing = false;
    while (auth._queue.length) auth._queue.shift()();
  } else {
    return new Promise(resolve => auth._queue.push(() => resolve(httpClient.request(opts))));
  }
  opts._alreadyRetried = true;
  return httpClient.request(opts);
}
```

devex-bot: CI issue recorded: https://ci.internal.redwood/gh/examples/next-starter-alt/9 -> tests/eval/parity -> 2419999985

Jared Lim: Can we add a guard so we only retry idempotent endpoints? Some LlamaIndex calls mutate state and a blind retry could double-post.

Samir Gupta: Good call. We should only auto-retry when opts.idempotent === true or method in SAFE_METHODS. I'll add a test that covers POST with idempotent flag and non-idempotent case.

Maya Patel: temporary unblock: set REDWOOD_SDK_ASSUME_RETRY=true in .env for CI to pass until we ship fix. Added note to CI job config.

Alex Chen: opened PR with queued-refresh implementation + unit tests + eval harness fixture (includes forced expiry test). PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-starter-alt/pull/12

Elena Rosa: I'll review PR. Also propose a tiny README addition in starter: how to simulate token expiry and set REDWOOD_SDK_ASSUME_RETRY during dev.

Samir Gupta: Also found a KV-cache header mismatch that caused 403 on some retries in the LlamaIndex sample; added a validation to only reattach cache headers after successful refresh.

Alex Chen: Merged PR after fixes. devex-bot: PR merged by Alex Chen at 2419999988 :shipit:

Maya Patel: confirmed parity harness passes locally. Thanks team! :tada:

Jared Lim: Will follow up with a small changelog entry and a migration note for users who rely on previous non-queueing behavior.

Alex Chen: Closing the loop: added migration note and toggles in README. If anyone hits regressions re-open thread.
